    "background_story": "Ahmed was a young artist living in a society where conformity was highly valued. Despite the pressure to fit in, he refused to compromise his creative vision. Ahmed's paintings were bold, unapologetic, and often challenged the status quo. His unservile spirit was evident in his refusal to cater to the tastes of wealthy patrons or government officials. Instead, he chose to create art that spoke truth to power and gave voice to the marginalized. Ahmed's unwavering commitment to his artistic integrity earned him both admiration and criticism. However, he remained steadfast, inspiring a new generation of artists to stand up for their freedom of expression and challenge the norms.",
